{"description":"Build the testing substrate the rest of the MVP depends on, because the behaviour that matters most here — reconnect, queue drain, presence expiry — is exactly the behaviour that is unreliable to verify by hand.\n\nThree parts: a deterministic network layer with injectable packet loss, latency and partition; a fake clock so timeouts and TTLs are exercised without waiting; and a null audio backend so continuous integration needs no sound hardware.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. Packet loss, added latency and network partition are all injectable per test.\n2. All timeouts, backoff intervals and TTLs are driven by the injectable clock; no test sleeps in real time.\n3. Tests are deterministic: the same seed produces the same execution, and the suite is not flaky under repeated runs.\n4. The null audio backend lets the audio-tagged build be tested with no sound device present.\n5. A twenty-client fleet can be simulated in one process, matching the real deployment's upper bound.\n6. Presence expiry, queue resumption and reconnect backoff each have coverage through this harness."}